# Hop ETL project guardrails

When creating or editing Hop pipelines/workflows in this repo:

1. Use `/design-hop-etl` for new pipelines; `/debug-hop-etl` for failures.
2. After design/debug work, follow `/learn-and-upgrade-hop-etl-skills` final step (NOOP if nothing new).
3. Run `.cursor/skills/design-hop-etl/scripts/validate-hpl.sh` on changed `.hpl` files before finishing.
4. TextFileInput2: require `<file>` with `<name>` + `<filemask>` and explicit `<fields>` — never empty `<files/>`.
5. Constant `batch_id`: `<value>${STAGING_BATCH_ID}</value>` and `<use_formatting>Y</use_formatting>`.
6. Variables and paths: `development_configs.json` — do not hardcode credentials.
7. Copy patterns from existing numbered pipeline folders (`01`–`09`); match naming conventions.
8. After Hop GUI saves, diff XML — GUI may strip `<value>`, `<file>`, or `<fields>`.
9. MDM: Hop Server `-e` uses lifecycle env `Hop_ETL_Test_Configs`; push needs Basic Auth + `X-API-Key`; test with `go run .` in `backend/`.
